# The demo, as requests: one story from an empty sale page to a sold item, with the refusals that keep it safe.
# Every route is in api-flash-be.http and api-flash-web.http; the replies are in docs/reference/http-endpoints.md.
#
# Before you start: `npm run demo:reset` (wipes the local data), `npm run demo:setup` (the operator `ops` and a sale of
# 3 items), then `npm run demo:dev`. The steps around this file are in docs/how-to/run-the-demo.md.
#
# The format is kulala.nvim (https://github.com/wahidyankf/kulala.nvim). Send the requests one at a time, from top to
# bottom: several show a refusal on purpose, and "run all" stops at the first one unless `halt_on_error` is false. A
# request named with `# @name` keeps its reply, and the requests after it read the sale id, the ticket and the
# reservation id from it, so nothing is copied by hand. The Shared block attaches kulala's cookie jar to every request,
# so a login is kept like in a browser.

### Shared
# @attach-cookie-jar
@backend = http://localhost:8080
@web = http://localhost:3000

###############################################################################
# Act 1. The API is up, and it checks what it depends on.
###############################################################################

### 1. Liveness: no dependencies, always 200
GET {{backend}}/health

### 2. Readiness: Postgres and Redis ("redis":"error" and 503 while Redis is stopped)
GET {{backend}}/ready

###############################################################################
# Act 2. The operator manages sales. Nobody can become an operator through the API; `ops` was made on the server.
###############################################################################

### 3. Log in as the operator (the tokens are in two HttpOnly cookies, never in the body)
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ops", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### 4. Create a sale for later (201)
# 409 sale_overlaps here means an earlier run stopped before 8: delete that sale (its id is in 6) and send 4 again.
# @name created
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Demo sale for later", "stock": 100, "startsAt": "2035-01-01T12:00:00Z", "endsAt": "2035-01-01T13:00:00Z" }

### 5. A second sale in the same hour: 409 sale_overlaps, one sale runs at a time
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 100, "startsAt": "2035-01-01T12:30:00Z", "endsAt": "2035-01-01T13:30:00Z" }

### 6. List every sale, with what only an operator sees (sold, holdSeconds, admitPerSecond)
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales

### 7. Give the new sale more stock (send only the fields that change)
PATCH {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 150 }

### 8. Remove the new sale (a soft delete: the row stays with deleted_at and deleted_by)
DELETE {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales/{{created.response.body.$.id}}

### 9. Log out the operator
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/auth/logout

###############################################################################
# Act 3. A shopper buys one item: queue, hold, pay. No route takes a user id: the shopper is the cookie's account.
###############################################################################

### 10. Sign up as a shopper (201; on a second run it answers 409 username_taken, so send 11)
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-demo", "password": "a long password" }

### 11. Log in as the shopper (only needed when 10 answered 409)
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-demo", "password": "a long password" }

### 12. The current sale: the running one, else the next to open
# @name current
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/current

### 13. Join the queue (201 with a signed ticket; "waiting" with a place, or "admitted")
# @name join
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue

### 14. Check the place (the queue admits shoppers each second; send again until "admitted")
# @delay 1500
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue/me
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### 15. Hold one item (201 with reservationId and expiresAt; the hold time comes from the sale)
# @name reserve
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/reservations
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### 16. Hold again: 200 with the same hold, never a second item
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/reservations
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### 17. Did I get it? "holding"
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases/me

### 18. Pay (201; the mock payment takes about 150 ms and declines about 2% of the time with 402, then send again)
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservationId": "{{reserve.response.body.$.reservationId}}" }

### 19. Pay again: 200 with the same purchase; the reservation id is the idempotency key, so one charge
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservationId": "{{reserve.response.body.$.reservationId}}" }

### 20. Did I get it? "purchased"
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases/me

### 21. A second item for the same shopper: 409 already_purchased (or sold_out, when 18 took the last item)
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/reservations
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### 22. The sale: remaining is one lower (reads are cached for up to a second)
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}

###############################################################################
# Act 4. What a shopper may not do.
###############################################################################

### 23. A shopper on an operator route: 403 forbidden
GET {{backend}}/api/v1/admin/sales

### 24. Log out
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### 25. Join with no login: 401 not_authenticated
POST {{backend}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue

###############################################################################
# Act 5. The browser talks only to flash-web, which passes on a fixed list of routes.
###############################################################################

### 26. The current sale through the web server (what the page reads)
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/current

### 27. The operator routes are not passed on: 404 not_found, and flash-be is not asked
GET {{web}}/api/v1/admin/sales

### 28. A path that is not on the list: 404 not_found, and flash-be is not asked
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/current/secret

### 29. A POST from another site: 403 cross_site
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/login
Origin: http://evil.example
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-demo", "password": "a long password" }

###############################################################################
# Act 6. Live updates: the page follows the sale without polling. curl closes the stream after 5 seconds here.
###############################################################################

### 30. Live sale status through the web server (event: sale)
# @accept chunked
# @curl-max-time 5
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/events
